WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.667 --> 00:00:02.869
-The house voted today

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.203
to strip Congresswoman
Marjorie Taylor Greene

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:07.139
of her committee assignments,
even as most Republicans

00:00:07.139 --> 00:00:09.208
stood by her,
despite a history

00:00:09.208 --> 00:00:11.010
of truly deranged,
bigoted statements.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.413
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:13.413 --> 00:00:17.517
♪♪

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:19.819
Right now, as we speak,
we're in the middle

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.420
of several urgent calamities

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:23.623
that show no signs of slowing
anytime soon.

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:25.658
Poverty and child hunger
are rising.

00:00:25.658 --> 00:00:27.293
Millions have lost
their health insurance

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.861
amid a deadly pandemic.

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:30.496
COVID variants are spreading.

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:32.898
Vaccinations are not keeping
pace with the spread.

00:00:32.898 --> 00:00:35.835
And on top of all of that,
pilots are saying

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:37.771
they're making
in-flight mistakes

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:39.605
because they're
so out of practice.

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:42.374
-CNN is learning that
some commercial airline pilots,

00:00:42.374 --> 00:00:45.644
the planes that fly all of us,
are telling federal authorities

00:00:45.644 --> 00:00:48.814
the long layoffs
and downtime during the pandemic

00:00:48.814 --> 00:00:51.584
has left them,
in their words, "rusty,"

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:54.287
causing them to even
make some in-flight mistakes.

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.623
-Pilots self-reported
being "rusty"

00:00:56.623 --> 00:01:00.793
in at least 26 separate cases
since the start of the pandemic.

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:03.529
-You never want to hear the
words "rusty"

00:01:03.529 --> 00:01:05.765
and "commercial airline pilot"
in the same sentence

00:01:05.765 --> 00:01:09.501
unless "rusty" is the name
of a commercial airline pilot.

00:01:09.501 --> 00:01:12.538
I mean, I would trust
a Captain Rusty with my life.

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:15.441
Oh, sure, sure,
there are some mornings

00:01:15.441 --> 00:01:18.578
when he's had a rough night
and has to blow out the cobwebs

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.045
before he takes her up.

00:01:20.045 --> 00:01:22.182
But when you lose an engine
and things go sideways,

00:01:22.182 --> 00:01:23.816
there's no one
I'd rather have at the helm

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.451
than Captain John Rustenberger.

00:01:25.451 --> 00:01:28.187
And the fact that you suits
at the FAA

00:01:28.187 --> 00:01:30.156
have the nerve to question him

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:33.359
when your idea of turbulence
is a Lexus going over a pothole,

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.728
well, it makes me
sick to my stomach!

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.397
Anyway, where was I?
Oh, right.

00:01:37.397 --> 00:01:39.966
Pilot is one of those jobs,
along with doctor

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:42.035
and crane operator
where you never want to be

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:43.269
"out of practice."

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:45.171
"Okay, folks, if you are seated

00:01:45.171 --> 00:01:46.606
on the right side
of the aircraft,

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:49.575
you can look out your window
and you'll see you are looking

00:01:49.575 --> 00:01:52.278
straight down at the ocean."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.278 --> 00:01:54.447
"Also, if anyone knows
what that alarm means,

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:58.150
go ahead and pop on by
the, uh, pilot house?

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.785
No, that's not it.
What is it?

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:02.454
Oh, the cockpit.
Knew it was something crazy.

00:02:02.454 --> 00:02:05.291
Why is it called that?

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.326
If you guys have
Gogo Internet Wi-Fi,

00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:09.629
could you google
why we call it the cockpit?"

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:12.164
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.164 --> 00:02:16.402
"Also, do you guys pay
for Gogo all year?

00:02:16.402 --> 00:02:18.137
I'm asking
for a talk-show host."

00:02:18.137 --> 00:02:20.373
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.373 --> 00:02:23.276
We need a functional,
healthy political system

00:02:23.276 --> 00:02:25.378
that can respond to these crises

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:27.847
because they're causing misery
and suffering

00:02:27.847 --> 00:02:29.215
for millions of Americans.

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.017
And with Democrats
taking control of Congress

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.619
and the White House, there have
been some real glimmers of hope.

00:02:33.619 --> 00:02:35.488
They're not waiting
for permission from Republicans

00:02:35.488 --> 00:02:37.724
to do big, bold things
on everything from COVID relief

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.124
to immigration,
to the environment.

00:02:39.124 --> 00:02:40.426
And on top of all of that,

00:02:40.426 --> 00:02:42.261
thanks to a new
organizing resolution

00:02:42.261 --> 00:02:44.897
finally passed after weeks
of GOP obstruction,

00:02:44.897 --> 00:02:46.866
the Senate Budget Committee
has a new chairman

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.968
who has made clear
he has no interest

00:02:48.968 --> 00:02:51.003
in yielding
to Republican stonewalling.

00:02:51.003 --> 00:02:53.940
-This formalizes the reality
that the Democrats

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:56.509
are now the majority party
in the United States Senate.

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:59.845
Because we're in a 50/50 split,
we need to have an agreement

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:02.081
over things like
how committees would be run.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:04.650
You heard from Leader Schumer
there, the deal is done.

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:06.152
It'll be voted on today.

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.620
That means, you know,
Bernie Sanders

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:09.087
is your new budget chairman.

00:03:09.087 --> 00:03:11.023
-That's right, Bernie's
in charge of the budget now.

00:03:11.023 --> 00:03:14.326
Get ready for direct checks,
expanded unemployment benefits,

00:03:14.326 --> 00:03:17.463
a $15 minimum wage,
and for the Senate thermostat

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:20.767
to be set to 64, no matter
how cold it is outside.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:23.469
"You're wasting heat.
Everyone gets a coat

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.772
and pair of mittens,
and if you're still cold,

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.139
try thinking warm thoughts.

00:03:27.139 --> 00:03:30.209
I like to picture a kitten
sharing her yarn

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:31.711
with other kittens
because no kitten

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.812
should lack access to yarn."

00:03:33.812 --> 00:03:35.815
As we've said many times
on this show,

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:38.217
there are massive systemic,
deeply engrained flaws

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:40.219
in our system
that preceded Donald Trump

00:03:40.219 --> 00:03:41.354
and will outlast him.

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:43.456
He exposed them
and made them worse,

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:44.891
but he did not create them.

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:46.925
And they won't just magically
go away now that he's gone.

00:03:46.925 --> 00:03:49.328
In fact,
he's not even really gone.

00:03:49.328 --> 00:03:51.597
He's still exerting influence
over the Republican Party.

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:54.867
Just last week, he met with
house GOP leader Kevin McCarthy

00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:57.303
at Mar-A-Lago and posted
this photo where the two of them

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:59.305
look like they're about to ask

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:02.909
if you have a structured
settlement and need cash now.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.877
They look less
like personal injury lawyers

00:04:04.877 --> 00:04:07.747
and more like lawyers
with personal injuries.

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:09.915
"Did you slip and fall
and land on your head?

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:11.150
Us too!

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:13.052
Do you need a lawyer?
So do we.

00:04:13.052 --> 00:04:15.254 line:0%
Call 1-800-1-Wait,
what's the number?

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:16.622 line:0%
I forgot.
Hold on, start over.

00:04:16.622 --> 00:04:18.257 line:0%
Who am I?"

00:04:18.257 --> 00:04:19.826
Also where are they?

00:04:19.826 --> 00:04:22.261
That looks like
a Miami drug lord's pool house.

00:04:22.261 --> 00:04:23.796
There should be a weird kid

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:26.031
lighting fire crackers
behind them.

00:04:26.031 --> 00:04:28.368
Even after he's left office,
Republicans are competing

00:04:28.368 --> 00:04:29.768
to prove their loyalty to Trump.

00:04:29.768 --> 00:04:32.237
Take, for example, Florida
Congressman Matt Gaetz,

00:04:32.237 --> 00:04:34.373
one of the seditionists
who spread lies

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:36.408
about election fraud and tried
to overthrow the results

00:04:36.408 --> 00:04:39.011
and who looks like someone
tried to make Tom Cruise

00:04:39.011 --> 00:04:41.848
out of Legos,
but then didn't have any Legos

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:44.783
so had to use Duplo bricks.

00:04:44.783 --> 00:04:46.385
He went on
Steve Bannon's podcast,

00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:49.155
which I assume he records
at the bottom of the sea.

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:51.790
Gaetz said he was so dedicated
to defending Trump

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:53.259
during the upcoming
impeachment trial

00:04:53.259 --> 00:04:55.561
that he'd be willing to give up
his Congressional seat

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:58.998
and even his house to join the
former president's defense team.

00:04:58.998 --> 00:05:01.434
-Would you resign in order
to defend the President

00:05:01.434 --> 00:05:03.035
on the way
that you want to defend him?

00:05:03.035 --> 00:05:05.871
-I love my district.
I love representing them.

00:05:05.871 --> 00:05:10.476
But I view this cancellation
of the Trump presidency

00:05:10.476 --> 00:05:15.181
and the Trump movement as one of
the major risks to my people,

00:05:15.181 --> 00:05:18.284
both in my district and all
throughout this great country.

00:05:18.284 --> 00:05:21.054
Absolutely,
if the President called me

00:05:21.054 --> 00:05:23.322
and wanted me to go defend him
on the floor of the Senate,

00:05:23.322 --> 00:05:25.624
that would be
the top priority in my life.

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:28.661
I would leave my House seat.
I would leave my home.

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:30.929
I would do anything I had to do.

00:05:30.929 --> 00:05:32.932
-"My House seat,
I would leave my home.

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:35.168
I would burn all my clothes
and give away all my money

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:36.969
because that's how much
I love this man.

00:05:36.969 --> 00:05:39.772
This man who has never returned
even an ounce

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.540
of the same loyalty
to anyone ever.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.643
I would do anything for him.
I would live in the woods.

00:05:43.643 --> 00:05:47.012
I would subsist on a diet
of squirrels and roughage.

00:05:47.012 --> 00:05:48.514
I'd roam through
the forest naked

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:50.483
looking for fraudulent ballots
like some sort of

00:05:50.483 --> 00:05:52.885
half man, half goblin,
scaring hikers

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:57.189
and feasting upon the garbage
left behind at campsites

00:05:57.189 --> 00:05:59.058
because that's how much
this man means to me,

00:05:59.058 --> 00:06:01.594
this man who is incapable
of human emotions

00:06:01.594 --> 00:06:04.096
like love and compassion who,
and this is true,

00:06:04.096 --> 00:06:05.898
once got my name wrong.

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:07.667
I would do anything for him."

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:10.102
I mean, it's just so hard
to fully articulate

00:06:10.102 --> 00:06:13.239
how pathetic it is to be that
servile toward any politician.

00:06:13.239 --> 00:06:14.673
I mean, do I like Joe Biden?

00:06:14.673 --> 00:06:15.941
Sure, I mean, I guess so.

00:06:15.941 --> 00:06:17.376
Would I quit my job
and leave my house

00:06:17.376 --> 00:06:19.178
to go defend him
if he got impeached for --

00:06:19.178 --> 00:06:21.213
I don't know
what he'd get impeached for.

00:06:21.213 --> 00:06:24.450
Like, getting in a fistfight
at a bar over a jukebox?

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:27.720
"Hey, who turned off
'Free Fallin'?

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:31.657
Time for you to meet Tom Petty
and the Face-Breakers."

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:33.892
But there's no doubt that
this is the wing of the party

00:06:33.892 --> 00:06:35.561
that's ascendant,
the Matt Gaetz,

00:06:35.561 --> 00:06:37.864
Marjorie Taylor Greene,
Donald Trump wing of the party.

00:06:37.864 --> 00:06:39.832
It doesn't matter if GOP
elder statesmen

00:06:39.832 --> 00:06:41.700
want to pretend they're
part of a nobler tradition

00:06:41.700 --> 00:06:43.135
of so-called conservatism.

00:06:43.135 --> 00:06:46.538
Utah Senator Mitt Romney
said this week of the GOP,

00:06:46.538 --> 00:06:49.008
"Our big tent
is not large enough

00:06:49.008 --> 00:06:51.777
to both accommodate
conservatives and kooks."

00:06:51.777 --> 00:06:55.280
Oh, buddy, you sound like a
middle school teacher who says,

00:06:55.280 --> 00:06:58.251
"Listen, we can't have
a pop quiz and a pizza party.

00:06:58.251 --> 00:06:59.885
So what's it gonna be, kids?

00:06:59.885 --> 00:07:03.289
Okay, I'm not hearing
a lot of 'pop quiz.'"

00:07:03.289 --> 00:07:05.658
Actually, your tent
is big enough for both.

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:08.126
Yesterday, House Republicans
voted to retain Liz Cheney

00:07:08.126 --> 00:07:11.630
in her leadership position and
gave Greene a standing ovation.

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:14.266
Your tent is big enough
for conservatives and kooks

00:07:14.266 --> 00:07:15.467
because it's a circus tent

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:17.870
or one of those large
outdoor wedding tents

00:07:17.870 --> 00:07:19.939
where you get speeches
from kindly grandpas

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:21.773
telling cute stories
about the bride

00:07:21.773 --> 00:07:24.076
and drunk aunts
who steal the mic

00:07:24.076 --> 00:07:25.344
and refuse to give it up.

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:26.946
"When I first saw
these two together,

00:07:26.946 --> 00:07:30.116
I knew there was a spark,
kind of like the spark

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:33.920
caused by the Jewish space laser
that started the wildfire.

00:07:33.920 --> 00:07:36.522
No! No, Pamela,
I will not sit down!

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:40.092
This is my time!
I'm being canceled!"

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:43.162
I'd tell Liz Cheney
to just leave the GOP,

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:46.265
but being a Cheney, I doubt
she has an exit strategy.

00:07:46.265 --> 00:07:48.734
Iraq War joke.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:48.734 --> 00:07:50.469
God, it's nice
now that Trump is gone

00:07:50.469 --> 00:07:53.038
and I can get back
to doing my Cheney material.

00:07:53.038 --> 00:07:55.207
It's a real shot in the face.

00:07:55.207 --> 00:07:58.310
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.310 --> 00:08:00.279
Now, it's worth stepping back
and remembering

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:02.715
that these people are massively
unpopular with normal people.

00:08:02.715 --> 00:08:04.449
Trump was, according to polling,

00:08:04.449 --> 00:08:06.351
the most disliked president
in modern history.

00:08:06.351 --> 00:08:09.154
He never cracked 50%,
lost the popular vote twice,

00:08:09.154 --> 00:08:10.355
got impeached twice,

00:08:10.355 --> 00:08:12.625
lost the House
by a record margin in 2018

00:08:12.625 --> 00:08:15.094
then lost the Senate,
not to mention he oversaw

00:08:15.094 --> 00:08:18.296
the worst public-health crisis
and economic crash in 100 years.

00:08:18.296 --> 00:08:21.066
Meanwhile, every single
executive order Joe Biden

00:08:21.066 --> 00:08:23.970
has issued so far that's been
the subject of polling

00:08:23.970 --> 00:08:26.605
has either majority
or plurality support,

00:08:26.605 --> 00:08:28.440
and even a majority
of Republicans

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.176
support the $1,400 checks.

00:08:30.176 --> 00:08:32.511
If we had an actual democracy
with a level playing field,

00:08:32.511 --> 00:08:33.846
Republicans would wield power

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:35.480
as often as the Jets
make the playoffs.

00:08:35.480 --> 00:08:38.083
They'd tank every year
but then win just enough games

00:08:38.083 --> 00:08:40.186
to lose out
on the top draft pick

00:08:40.186 --> 00:08:42.387
and get stuck with some
second-tier quarterback

00:08:42.387 --> 00:08:45.024
from one of those super specific
part of the state schools

00:08:45.024 --> 00:08:47.826
you've never been to,
like Southwest Idaho Tech

00:08:47.826 --> 00:08:50.562
or Northeastern Montana A&amp;M,
a guy with an unforgettable name

00:08:50.562 --> 00:08:54.900
like Matt Jones or Jake Smith
or just Steve.

00:08:54.900 --> 00:08:57.970
"I don't like this Steve guy!"

00:08:57.970 --> 00:08:59.772
In a normal democracy,
the Republican Party

00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:02.241
would be forced to dump all
these deeply unpopular goblins

00:09:02.241 --> 00:09:04.977
because they would have to
appeal to a majority of voters.

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:06.645
But we don't have
a normal democracy.

00:09:06.645 --> 00:09:08.881
We have a system where the GOP
has won the popular vote

00:09:08.881 --> 00:09:11.083
one time in the last 32 years

00:09:11.083 --> 00:09:13.552
and where the 50 Senate
Republicans represent

00:09:13.552 --> 00:09:16.755
40 million fewer Americans
than the 50 Senate Democrats.

00:09:16.755 --> 00:09:20.859
So Republicans have no incentive
to appeal to most Americans,

00:09:20.859 --> 00:09:23.829
only to their base, and their
base is increasingly unhinged.

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:27.199
New polls show that Republican
voters favor Greene and McCarthy

00:09:27.199 --> 00:09:29.568
over Cheney and McConnell,
despite the fact that Greene

00:09:29.568 --> 00:09:32.371
has said, among other things,
that school shootings were faked

00:09:32.371 --> 00:09:34.874
and that Nancy Pelosi
should be executed for treason,

00:09:34.874 --> 00:09:36.809
questioned whether a plane
crashed into the Pentagon

00:09:36.809 --> 00:09:39.411
on 9/11, and suggested
that a Jewish space laser

00:09:39.411 --> 00:09:40.612
caused wildfires.

00:09:40.612 --> 00:09:42.882
I know we keep mentioning
the space laser,

00:09:42.882 --> 00:09:44.549
and it does sound insane
out of context.

00:09:44.549 --> 00:09:46.385
But it's worth actually
reading what she said.

00:09:46.385 --> 00:09:49.788
This is what Greene wrote
in a 2018 Facebook post,

00:09:49.788 --> 00:09:54.126
when, to be fair,
she was only in her early 40s.

00:10:19.885 --> 00:10:23.022
Anytime someone says there are
too many coincidences to ignore

00:10:23.022 --> 00:10:24.556
and their name isn't Fox Mulder,

00:10:24.556 --> 00:10:26.492
that's your cue
to exit the conversation.

00:10:26.492 --> 00:10:28.194
It's like wandering over
to someone and hearing,

00:10:28.194 --> 00:10:30.830
"Look, I'm not saying dolphins
definitely are secret agents

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:32.464
trained by the CIA to spy on us.

00:10:32.464 --> 00:10:34.967
I'm just asking why are they
always jumping out of the water?

00:10:34.967 --> 00:10:36.668
What's so interesting up here

00:10:36.668 --> 00:10:38.203
that they just
have to look at it?

00:10:38.203 --> 00:10:41.173
Why are they always smiling like
someone just told them a secret?

00:10:41.173 --> 00:10:43.942
Also, the way they click,
that's Jewish Morse code.

00:10:43.942 --> 00:10:46.579
Oh, got to go.
Time for my wedding toast.

00:10:46.579 --> 00:10:49.147
Don't side-eye me, Pamela!"

00:10:49.147 --> 00:10:51.316
And yet despite her history
of expressing support

00:10:51.316 --> 00:10:53.419
for political violence
as well as anti-Muslim

00:10:53.419 --> 00:10:55.321
and anti-Semitic
conspiracy theories,

00:10:55.321 --> 00:10:57.890
yesterday, McCarthy
basically stood by Greene

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:59.357
and claimed she'd apologized.

00:10:59.357 --> 00:11:03.629
-I denounced all of those
comments that were brought up.

00:11:03.629 --> 00:11:05.898
Everybody --
And she came to the --

00:11:05.898 --> 00:11:09.501
She came inside our conference
and denounced them, as well.

00:11:09.501 --> 00:11:11.103
She said she was wrong.

00:11:11.103 --> 00:11:13.572
She has reached out
in other ways and forms.

00:11:13.572 --> 00:11:16.709
She has expressed
that she has put it out

00:11:16.709 --> 00:11:19.145
from news agencies and others,
I think it would be helpful

00:11:19.145 --> 00:11:21.647
if you could hear exactly
what she told all of us.

00:11:21.647 --> 00:11:24.082
Denouncing Q-on.
I don't know if I say it right.

00:11:24.082 --> 00:11:26.318
I don't even know what it is.

00:11:26.318 --> 00:11:28.454
Any from the shootings,
she said she knew nothing

00:11:28.454 --> 00:11:30.589
about lasers
or all of the different things

00:11:30.589 --> 00:11:32.091
that have been brought up
about her.

00:11:32.091 --> 00:11:35.227
-Okay. First of all, you don't
know how to pronounce QAnon?

00:11:35.227 --> 00:11:37.162
Isn't that exactly
what a Deep State

00:11:37.162 --> 00:11:39.198
Satanic cult member would say?

00:11:39.198 --> 00:11:42.167
Sorry. There are just too many
coincidences to ignore.

00:11:42.167 --> 00:11:43.535
Second,
you should probably learn

00:11:43.535 --> 00:11:45.203
since a lot of your voters
are super into it.

00:11:45.203 --> 00:11:46.772
That's like Kid Rock saying,
"I'm sorry.

00:11:46.772 --> 00:11:50.376
How do you pronounce this?
Ba wit daba?"

00:11:50.376 --> 00:11:52.777
Second, if you want us
to hear her say it,

00:11:52.777 --> 00:11:54.179
then why doesn't
she just say it?

00:11:54.179 --> 00:11:55.781
If she's so sincere
about her apology,

00:11:55.781 --> 00:11:57.082
then why doesn't
she make it public?

00:11:57.082 --> 00:11:59.785
Is it a secret?
Is this like when you forget

00:11:59.785 --> 00:12:01.287
to buy your wife
an anniversary gift

00:12:01.287 --> 00:12:04.790
and you tell her you have one
but you can't show it to her yet

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:06.424
because it's too good
and she needs

00:12:06.424 --> 00:12:07.859
to mentally prepare for it,
and then you spend

00:12:07.859 --> 00:12:09.995
the rest of the night typing
"things my wife likes"

00:12:09.995 --> 00:12:13.932
into Amazon until Amazon types
back, "I'm not her husband!"?

00:12:13.932 --> 00:12:16.101
She obviously is not sincere.

00:12:16.101 --> 00:12:17.736
She's been raising money off it.

00:12:17.736 --> 00:12:19.338
And then, today she spoke
on the House floor,

00:12:19.338 --> 00:12:21.540
where instead
of apologizing unequivocally

00:12:21.540 --> 00:12:23.141
and denouncing
her previous comments,

00:12:23.141 --> 00:12:24.543
the best she could do was this.

00:12:24.543 --> 00:12:28.113
-I also want to tell you
9/11 absolutely happened.

00:12:28.113 --> 00:12:29.147
-Oh, my God, thank you.

00:12:29.147 --> 00:12:31.150
It is so big of you
to admit that.

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:32.885
What else would you
like to clarify?

00:12:32.885 --> 00:12:33.985
"I would also like to make clear

00:12:33.985 --> 00:12:35.787
that 'Inception'
is just a movie,

00:12:35.787 --> 00:12:39.825
RoboCop is not real, and the
giant glowing orb in the sky

00:12:39.825 --> 00:12:43.261
is in fact the Moon
and not a secret sky bank

00:12:43.261 --> 00:12:45.463
where Bill Gates
keeps all his gold bars."

00:12:45.463 --> 00:12:48.234
Then she went back to saying
more heinous stuff

00:12:48.234 --> 00:12:50.702
like equating the media
with QAnon.

00:12:50.702 --> 00:12:55.541
-Will we allow the media,
that is just as guilty as QAnon,

00:12:55.541 --> 00:12:58.743
of presenting
truth and lies to divide us?

00:12:58.743 --> 00:13:00.645
-Are you insane?
Wait. I'm sorry.

00:13:00.645 --> 00:13:02.248
Why am I asking this
as a question?

00:13:02.248 --> 00:13:04.650
You are insane.
"The media and QAnon

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:06.251
are both guilty
of dividing Americans

00:13:06.251 --> 00:13:08.987
by claiming a secret cabal of
baby-eating Satan worshippers

00:13:08.987 --> 00:13:10.789
is running the government.
Wolf Blitzer,

00:13:10.789 --> 00:13:14.260
I accept your apology,
if that is your real name.

00:13:14.260 --> 00:13:18.764
I see you under that beard,
space laser."

00:13:18.764 --> 00:13:20.966
Nicely done
on the graphic there.

00:13:20.966 --> 00:13:23.202
I had no idea what
it was gonna look like.

00:13:23.202 --> 00:13:26.172
Kind of a fun little payoff.

00:13:26.172 --> 00:13:27.739
The Republican Party
is radicalizing

00:13:27.739 --> 00:13:29.908
against democracy and away
from the political mainstream

00:13:29.908 --> 00:13:31.410
because it has no incentive
to appeal

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:32.711
to a majority of Americans.

00:13:32.711 --> 00:13:34.613
That's why we need far-reaching
structural reforms

00:13:34.613 --> 00:13:37.049
to our democracy
to level the playing field.

00:13:37.049 --> 00:13:39.351
A system where one party
can yield power

00:13:39.351 --> 00:13:41.619
despite representing
40 million fewer Americans

00:13:41.619 --> 00:13:43.822
in the Senate and winning
the presidential popular vote

00:13:43.822 --> 00:13:45.858
once in 32 years is not tenable.

00:13:45.858 --> 00:13:47.392
Because right now,
we have one party

00:13:47.392 --> 00:13:49.694
that's based in reality
and another that believes in --

00:13:49.694 --> 00:13:50.863
-Lasers.

00:13:50.863 --> 00:13:52.698
